= The King forces a vote

Months have passed without a candidate facing the chamber, and without a first vote the constitutional clock cannot start. The King proposes [+ right_leader +] once more, and this time the vote goes ahead.

[? if acting = 1 : He loses it. The two-month clock has started: if no one is invested, the Cortes will be dissolved and Spain will vote again. ?][? if acting = 0 : He wins it. Spain has a government. ?]

@morning_after
title: The morning after
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: elections_held >= 1 and morning_seen = 0
on-arrival: morning_seen = 1

= 21 December 2015 — The morning after

The results are in. Your senior team gathers at Ferraz. The party faces two opposite accusations: that it will rescue the PP, or that it will hand the country to Podemos. Regional presidents, former leaders and the parliamentary group all have their own ideas about what you should do next.

How do you position the PSOE this morning?

- @responsible: The responsible opposition: no to [+ pp_leader_short +], no promises yet
- @alternative: An alternative government: announce talks for a change of government
- @stability: Institutional stability: explore whether any agreement with the PP is possible

@responsible
on-arrival: posture = 1; sanchez_authority += 2; member_morale += 3; regional_leaders_dissent -= 3

Refusing to back [+ pp_leader_short +] while keeping every other door open reassures anti-PP voters and most of the party. Your critics will call it indecision.

@alternative
on-arrival: {! Q.posture = 2; Q.rel_up += 10; Q.rel_cs -= 6; Q.member_morale += 7; Q.progressives_dissent -= 5; Q.regional_leaders_dissent += 8; Q.institutionalists_dissent += 4; Q.sanchez_authority += 3; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.transfer(Q, 'up', 'psoe', {workers: 1, students: 1}); window.SpainGame.transfer(Q, 'psoe', 'cs', {pensioners: 0.5, self_employed: 0.5}); } if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.position(Q, 0.8, 0); } !}

The members are energised. In Seville, Toledo and Mérida, regional presidents read the announcement with alarm.

@stability
on-arrival: {! Q.posture = 3; Q.rel_pp += 10; Q.rel_cs += 5; Q.member_morale -= 8; Q.progressives_dissent += 8; Q.institutionalists_dissent -= 5; Q.regional_leaders_dissent -= 3; Q.sanchez_authority -= 3; if (Q.campaign_line == 1) { Q.sanchez_authority -= 4; Q.member_morale -= 6; } if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.transfer(Q, 'up', {workers: Q.campaign_line == 1 ? 2.5 : 1.5, students: 1.5, unemployed: 1}); } if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.position(Q, -0.8, 0); } !}

Institutional voices welcome your responsibility. Among the members, the word "abstention" is already circulating. [? if campaign_line = 1 : You promised in the campaign that the PSOE would never make Rajoy Prime Minister, and the members have not forgotten. ?]

@gurtel
title: The Gürtel sentence
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: gurtel_seen = 0 and ((year = 2018 and month >= 5) or year >= 2019)
on-arrival: {!
Q.gurtel_seen = 1;
Q.pp_scandal = (Q.pp_scandal || 0) + 3;
if (window.SpainGame) {
    window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'pp', {pensioners: -3, professionals: -3, self_employed: -2, workers: -2, homemakers: -2});
}
!}

= The Gürtel sentence

The National Court rules that the People's Party profited from the Gürtel corruption network, and finds that the PP ran a parallel accounting system for years. [? if pp_governs = 1 : Rajoy is Prime Minister of a government whose party has just been convicted as a beneficiary of corruption. Every opposition party is asking the same question: who will table a motion of no confidence? ?][? if pp_governs = 0 : The PP, out of government, takes the blow in the polls. ?]

@cat_referendum_law
title: The referendum laws
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: cat_crisis_seen = 0 and catalonia_independentist = 1 and ((year = 2017 and month >= 9) or year >= 2018)
on-arrival: {!
Q.cat_crisis_seen = 1; Q.catalan_crisis = 1; Q.cat_crisis_stage = 1; Q.cat_stage_time = Q.time;
if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.partyRel(Q, 'cs', 'erc', -5); window.SpainGame.partyRel(Q, 'cs', 'junts', -8); window.SpainGame.partyRel(Q, 'pp', 'junts', -10); window.SpainGame.partyRel(Q, 'pnv', 'junts', 5); }
if (window.SpainGame) {
    window.SpainGame.territorial(Q, 'Cataluña', 'erc', 1.1);
    window.SpainGame.territorial(Q, 'Cataluña', 'junts', 1.1);
    window.SpainGame.regionalMod(Q, 'Cataluña', 'cs', 1.25);
    window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'vox', {self_employed: 1.5, pensioners: 1, workers: 1, homemakers: 1});
    window.SpainGame.recalculate(Q);
}
!}

= The referendum laws

In two chaotic sessions, the Parliament of Catalonia passes a law calling a referendum on independence for 1 October and a "transitional law" for a new republic. The opposition walks out. The Constitutional Court suspends both laws within days. [? if psoe_in_government = 1 : As Prime Minister, the response is yours to lead. ?][? if psoe_in_government = 0 : Rajoy's government asks the PSOE for unity in defence of the Constitution. ?]

A new deck of cards is available: **Catalan crisis**.

- @state: Stand with the State: the law must be enforced
- @both: Defend the law, and call for dialogue at the same time
- @talk: Insist that only negotiation can solve this

@state
on-arrival: rel_cs += 5; rel_pp += 5; rel_erc -= 15; rel_junts -= 15; regional_leaders_dissent -= 8; progressives_dissent += 5; cat_hard_line += 1

You stand beside the institutions. Miquel Iceta's PSC warns that the PSOE must not disappear from Catalan politics.

@both
on-arrival: cat_dialogue += 1; regional_leaders_dissent += 2; sanchez_authority += 2

Defend the Constitution, offer a way out. Neither side is convinced, but both keep talking to you.

@talk
on-arrival: {! Q.cat_dialogue += 2; Q.rel_erc += 8; Q.rel_junts += 5; Q.rel_cs -= 10; Q.regional_leaders_dissent += 12; Q.institutionalists_dissent += 6; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.position(Q, 0, 1); } !}

The PSC and Podemos welcome it. Susana Díaz and García-Page say it publicly: the PSOE cannot sound like it is negotiating with lawbreakers.

@cat_1o
title: 1 October
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: catalan_crisis = 1 and cat_crisis_stage = 1 and time >= cat_stage_time + 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.cat_crisis_stage = 2;
Q.cat_stage_time = Q.time;
if (window.SpainGame) {
    window.SpainGame.territorial(Q, 'Cataluña', 'erc', 1.08);
    window.SpainGame.territorial(Q, 'Cataluña', 'junts', 1.08);
    window.SpainGame.regionalMod(Q, 'Cataluña', 'cs', 1.15);
    window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'vox', {self_employed: 2, pensioners: 1.5, workers: 1.5, homemakers: 1, professionals: 1});
    window.SpainGame.recalculate(Q);
}
!}

= 1 October

The referendum goes ahead without legal guarantees. Police try to stop the voting in hundreds of polling stations; the images of baton charges travel round the world. The Catalan government claims 90% voted yes on a turnout of 43%. Two days later, the King addresses the nation.

- @back_police: Back the State's response without reservation
- @criticise: Defend legality but criticise the police charges
- @mediate: Call for mediation and an urgent meeting of the party leaders

@back_police
on-arrival: rel_pp += 4; rel_cs += 4; rel_up -= 6; rel_erc -= 10; regional_leaders_dissent -= 5; progressives_dissent += 6; cat_hard_line += 1

Order before everything. In Barcelona, PSC mayors take down their posters.

@criticise
on-arrival: rel_up += 3; rel_erc += 3; regional_leaders_dissent += 3; sanchez_authority += 1

You keep a foot in both camps, and are attacked from both.

@mediate
on-arrival: {! Q.cat_dialogue += 1; Q.rel_erc += 6; Q.rel_junts += 4; Q.rel_pp -= 6; Q.regional_leaders_dissent += 8; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.position(Q, 0, 0.8); } !}

Mediation goes nowhere, but you are the only national leader still talking to everyone.

@cat_155
title: Independence and Article 155
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: catalan_crisis = 1 and cat_crisis_stage = 2 and time >= cat_stage_time + 1 and psoe_in_government = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.cat_crisis_stage = 3;
if (Q.regions && Q.regions['Cataluña']) {
    var y = Q.year, m = Q.month + 2;
    if (m > 12) { m -= 12; y += 1; }
    Q.regions['Cataluña'].nextElection = y + '-' + (m < 10 ? '0' : '') + m + '-21';
    Q.regions['Cataluña'].lastWasSnap = true;
}
!}

= Independence and Article 155

The Parliament of Catalonia votes a declaration of independence. Within hours, the Senate authorises the use of Article 155 of the Constitution: the Catalan government is dismissed and Catalan elections are called for two months' time. Puigdemont leaves for Brussels; members of his government are jailed pending trial.

- @support_155: Support Article 155, limited to calling elections
- @abstain_155: Refuse to support it: politics, not courts and police
- @own_155: Support it, and demand a commission on constitutional reform in exchange

@support_155
on-arrival: {! Q.rel_pp += 6; Q.rel_cs += 6; Q.rel_erc -= 15; Q.rel_junts -= 20; Q.rel_up -= 8; Q.regional_leaders_dissent -= 10; Q.progressives_dissent += 8; Q.cat_hard_line += 1; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'psoe', {pensioners: 1, homemakers: 0.5}); window.SpainGame.regionalMod(Q, 'Cataluña', 'psoe', 0.96); } !}

The PSOE stands with the State. The PSC's vote holds in Barcelona's suburbs and falls in Girona.

@abstain_155
on-arrival: {! Q.rel_pp -= 10; Q.rel_cs -= 10; Q.rel_erc += 6; Q.rel_up += 6; Q.regional_leaders_dissent += 25; Q.institutionalists_dissent += 15; Q.federal_committee_balance -= 8; Q.sanchez_authority -= 4; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.transfer(Q, 'psoe', {cs: 0.5, pp: 0.4, vox: 0.1}, {pensioners: 2.5, homemakers: 2, self_employed: 1.5, workers: 1}); window.SpainGame.regionalMod(Q, 'Cataluña', 'psoe', 1.06); } if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.position(Q, 0, 1.5); } !}

The barons call it a betrayal of the Constitution. Podemos and the PSC applaud; nobody else does.

@own_155
on-arrival: rel_pp += 3; rel_cs += 3; rel_erc -= 8; regional_leaders_dissent -= 4; sanchez_authority += 3; constitutional_commission = 1

You get your commission on reforming the territorial model, on paper. It keeps the federal idea alive.

@cat_crisis_end
title: After the Catalan election
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: catalan_crisis = 1 and cat_crisis_stage = 3 and cat_election_held = 1
on-arrival: catalan_crisis = 0; cat_crisis_stage = 4

= After the Catalan election

Catalonia has voted. The direct rule of Article 155 ends with the new government, but the crisis has changed Spanish politics: Ciudadanos rode it in Catalonia, and a small party called Vox has made itself known as a private prosecutor in the courts against the independence leaders.

The Catalan crisis deck is closed for now. The questions it raised are not.

@vox_vistalegre
title: Vox fills Vistalegre
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: cat_crisis_seen = 1 and vox_rise_seen = 0 and ((year = 2018 and month >= 10) or year >= 2019)
on-arrival: {!
Q.vox_rise_seen = 1;
// The surge feeds on the Catalan crisis: on dialogue the right calls weakness,
// and on how far the PP has itself moved to the right.
var push = 8 + 2 * (Q.cat_dialogue || 0) - (Q.cat_hard_line || 0) + (Q.pp_scandal >= 3 ? 2 : 0);
push = Math.max(3, push);
Q.vox_push = push;
if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.partyRel(Q, 'pp', 'vox', 10); window.SpainGame.partyRel(Q, 'cs', 'vox', 5); }
if (window.SpainGame) {
    window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'vox', {self_employed: push + 3, pensioners: push - 1, workers: push,
        homemakers: push - 1, professionals: push - 2, unemployed: push - 1, students: push - 2});
    window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'pp', {self_employed: -2, pensioners: -1});
    window.SpainGame.recalculate(Q);
}
!}

= Vox fills Vistalegre

Ten thousand people pack the Vistalegre arena in Madrid, and thousands more are turned away, for a party that won 0.2% of the vote in 2015. Santiago Abascal promises to suspend Catalan autonomy, deport illegal immigrants and repeal the gender-violence law.

[? if cat_dialogue >= 3 : Abascal's loudest applause comes when he attacks the "dialogue with coup plotters". ?][? if cat_hard_line >= 3 : The State's firmness in Catalonia has taken some of the wind out of his sails, but not all of it. ?]

The polls start to pick it up. Vox is no longer a curiosity.

@brussels
title: A letter from Brussels
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: brussels_due = 1 and psoe_in_government = 1
on-arrival: {! Q.brussels_year = Q.year; Q.brussels_due = 0; !}

= A letter from Brussels

The European Commission writes that Spain's deficit, [+ deficit_text +]% of GDP, breaches the Stability and Growth Pact's 3% ceiling. It asks for "additional measures".

- @cuts: Announce spending cuts
- @taxes: Raise taxes on large companies and banks
- @defy_brussels: Defend your spending: growth will close the gap

@cuts
on-arrival: {! Q.fiscal_adj -= 0.5; Q.progressives_dissent += 6; Q.trade_unionists_dissent += 6; Q.rel_up -= 6; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'psoe', {workers: -1.5, pensioners: -1, unemployed: -1}); window.SpainGame.recalculate(Q); } if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.position(Q, -1.5, 0); } !}

The Commission is satisfied. Your voters remember 2010.

@taxes
on-arrival: {! Q.fiscal_adj -= 0.4; Q.rel_cs -= 6; Q.rel_pp -= 4; Q.rel_up += 4; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'psoe', {self_employed: -1, professionals: -0.5}); window.SpainGame.recalculate(Q); } if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.position(Q, 1, 0); } !}

The banks protest; the Commission accepts the plan.

@defy_brussels
on-arrival: {! Q.sanchez_authority -= 4; Q.institutionalists_dissent += 6; Q.fiscal_adj += 0.1; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.recalculate(Q); } !}

The risk premium rises a few points. The Commission keeps writing.

@gallardon
title: The abortion law falls
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: gallardon_seen = 0 and ((year = 2014 and month >= 9) or year >= 2015) and pp_governs = 1
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: gallardon_seen = 1

= The abortion law falls

Facing protests across the country and divisions in his own party, Rajoy withdraws the justice minister's law restricting abortion. Alberto Ruiz-Gallardón resigns.

- @women_victory: Celebrate it as a victory for women's mobilisation
- @repeal: Promise to restore the 2010 law in full, including for 16- and 17-year-olds
- @move_on: Move on: this was the PP's own mess

@women_victory
on-arrival: {! Q.progressives_dissent -= 3; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.target(Q, 'psoe', 'women', 2.5); window.SpainGame.recalculate(Q); } if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.position(Q, 0, 0.5); } !}

The feminist organisations that led the protests welcome the PSOE's support.

@repeal
on-arrival: {! Q.progressives_dissent -= 5; Q.institutionalists_dissent += 2; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.target(Q, 'psoe', 'women', 2); window.SpainGame.target(Q, 'psoe', 'young', 1.5); window.SpainGame.target(Q, 'psoe', 'pensioners', -1); window.SpainGame.recalculate(Q); } if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.position(Q, 0, 1.2); } !}

A clear commitment. The bishops' conference condemns it.

@move_on
on-arrival: institutionalists_dissent -= 2

The PP's divisions speak for themselves.

@black_cards
title: The black cards and Púnica
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: black_cards_seen = 0 and ((year = 2014 and month >= 10) or year >= 2015)
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: {! Q.black_cards_seen = 1; Q.pp_scandal = (Q.pp_scandal || 0) + 1; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'pp', {pensioners: -1, professionals: -1.5, self_employed: -1}); } !}

= The black cards and Púnica

Two scandals in one month. The board of Caja Madrid, the savings bank rescued with public money, spent millions on undeclared "black" credit cards: the users include PP figures, but also PSOE and IU representatives and union leaders. Days later, Operation Púnica arrests dozens of mayors and officials, most of them from the PP, for kickbacks on public contracts.

Disgust with "the caste" of the old parties has never been higher.

- @expel: Expel every PSOE member who used a black card, immediately
- @anticorruption: Propose a state pact against corruption
- @attack_pp: Focus on the PP: it is their system

@expel
on-arrival: {! Q.sanchez_authority += 5; Q.institutionalists_dissent += 5; Q.trade_unionists_dissent += 4; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.target(Q, 'psoe', 'middle', 1.5); window.SpainGame.target(Q, 'psoe', 'young', 1); window.SpainGame.recalculate(Q); } !}

You act within hours. Some veterans think you threw old comrades to the wolves; the voters think you did the obvious thing.

@anticorruption
on-arrival: {! Q.rel_cs += 4; Q.rel_pp -= 2; Q.institutionalists_dissent -= 2; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.target(Q, 'psoe', 'middle', 1); window.SpainGame.recalculate(Q); } !}

A serious proposal. Rajoy ignores it; the new parties call it too little, too late.

@attack_pp
on-arrival: {! Q.rel_pp -= 6; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.transfer(Q, 'psoe', 'up', {students: 1, workers: 0.5}); } !}

The PSOE's own cardholders are still on the front pages. Podemos says "PP and PSOE, the same thing".

@vistalegre_podemos
title: Podemos at Vistalegre
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: podemos_assembly_seen = 0 and ((year = 2014 and month >= 10) or year >= 2015)
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: podemos_assembly_seen = 1

= Podemos at Vistalegre

Seven thousand people fill the Vistalegre arena for Podemos's founding assembly. Pablo Iglesias wins control of the party and sets one goal: to "storm the heavens" and govern Spain. Within weeks, some polls put Podemos first.

How does the PSOE answer?

- @compete_left: Compete for the same voters: a bold programme for the young and the precarious
- @populists: Call it what it is: populism with simple answers
- @own_ground: Ignore Podemos and talk about governing

@compete_left
on-arrival: {! Q.progressives_dissent -= 4; Q.rel_up -= 2; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.target(Q, 'psoe', 'young', 2.5); window.SpainGame.target(Q, 'psoe', 'unemployed', 2); window.SpainGame.recalculate(Q); } if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.position(Q, 0.8, 0); } !}

You will not leave the indignant generation to Iglesias. Some of them listen.

@populists
on-arrival: {! Q.rel_up -= 12; Q.regional_leaders_dissent -= 4; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.target(Q, 'psoe', 'pensioners', 2); window.SpainGame.transfer(Q, 'psoe', 'up', {students: 1.5, unemployed: 1}); } if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.position(Q, -0.5, 0); } !}

Older voters nod. Younger ones hear the establishment defending itself.

@own_ground
on-arrival: institutionalists_dissent -= 2; modernisers_dissent += 2

You keep your distance. Podemos keeps growing.

@nine_n
title: The 9N consultation
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: nine_n_seen = 0 and ((year = 2014 and month >= 11) or year >= 2015)
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: {! Q.nine_n_seen = 1; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.regionalMod(Q, 'Cataluña', 'cs', 1.15); window.SpainGame.recalculate(Q); } !}

= The 9N consultation

Despite the Constitutional Court, Artur Mas's government holds a "participatory process" on independence. 2.3 million Catalans vote, 80% of them for independence; most of those who oppose it stay at home. In Catalonia, Ciudadanos becomes the loudest voice against the process.

- @federal_answer: Answer with the federal reform of the Constitution
- @legal_answer: Back legal action against the consultation
- @psc_space: Let the PSC find its own space

@federal_answer
on-arrival: {! Q.federal_proposal = 1; Q.rel_pnv += 3; Q.regional_leaders_dissent += 3; Q.cat_dialogue += 1; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.position(Q, 0, 0.5); } !}

The Granada Declaration becomes your answer: a federal Spain. Few in Catalonia are listening any more.

@legal_answer
on-arrival: {! Q.rel_pp += 3; Q.regional_leaders_dissent -= 4; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.regionalMod(Q, 'Cataluña', 'psoe', 0.97); window.SpainGame.recalculate(Q); } !}

The barons approve. The PSC loses more members to the independence camp.

@psc_space
on-arrival: {! Q.sanchez_authority -= 1; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.regionalMod(Q, 'Cataluña', 'psoe', 1.02); window.SpainGame.recalculate(Q); } !}

Miquel Iceta's PSC treads its own careful line.

@diaz_snap
title: Díaz calls an election
new-page: true
